<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps rates Mexico 10-yr issue as Double B.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps rates Mexico 10-yr issue as Double B.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co on Thursday said it assigned a Double B foreign currency rating to a 500 billion Italian lire bond issue from Mexico.</p>
<p>The 10-year bonds have a 9.22 percent coupon.</p>
<p>This bond issue improves Mexico's debt profile by reducing costs, extending maturity and broadening its investor base, Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>Short-term amortizations outstanding for 1997, 1998 and 1999 have been reduced by more than $5 billion since September 1995, while gross international reserves have nearly tripled to US$18.1 billion from US$6.1 billion at the end of 1994, the rating agency said.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
